    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an expanded draft:\n\nDear Remote Team,\n\nAs we continue to work remotely, we want to ensure that you maintain a comfortable and safe working environment, which is essential for your overall well-being and productivity. Unfortunately, we've noticed an increase in complaints about wrist pain and back aches, and we want to address these issues proactively.\n\nMany of these discomforts can be prevented or reduced with a few simple adjustments to your workspace. To help you set up your home office for ergonomics, please consider the following guidelines:\n\n- Place your monitor directly in front of you, at a distance of about 20-25 inches, and at a height that allows you to gaze slightly downward (about 2-3 inches below eye level).\n- Adjust your chair height so that your feet are flat on the floor or on a footrest, with your knees at or below hip level.\n- Position your keyboard directly in front of your body, with wrists straight and elbows at a 90-degree angle.\n- Keep your mouse close to your body, with your wrist straight and arm relaxed.\n- Consider using a document holder to keep your papers or documents at eye level, reducing the need to constantly look down or crane your neck.\n\nBy making these",
